### hogwarts-service: example requests (needs the demo data, demo.seed=true)
### Open in VS Code with the "REST Client" extension (or IntelliJ) and click "Send Request".
### Run them top to bottom: later requests reuse ids from earlier responses.

@api = http://localhost:8080/api

### 1. Wizard overview: house, wand, spells (favourite first) with spell details
# @name harry
GET {{api}}/views/wizard-overview?name=Harry%20Potter

### 2. Spell book: the many-to-many from the other side (spell -> casters -> wizard -> house)
# @name patronus
GET {{api}}/views/spell-book?name=Expecto%25

### 3. Every spell whose name ends in "Curse", and who casts it ("%" is encoded as %25)
GET {{api}}/views/spell-book?name=%25curse

### 4. House roster: students and professors (same table, discriminator "type")
GET {{api}}/views/house-roster

### 5. The same data through GraphQL, choosing the fields
POST http://localhost:8080/graphql
Content-Type: application/json

{ "query": "{ wizardOverview(nameLike: \"%Weasley\") { items { name patronus house { name } spells { level favourite spell { incantation } } } } }" }

### 6. Harry's favourite becomes the Patronus Charm: the SingleFavouriteSpell rule demotes Expelliarmus
PATCH {{api}}/wizards/{{harry.response.body.$.items[0].id}}/spells/{{patronus.response.body.$.items[0].id}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "favourite": true }

### 7. Check: only one favourite left
GET {{api}}/wizards/{{harry.response.body.$.items[0].id}}/spells

### 8. A new spell
# @name tickling
POST {{api}}/spells
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Tickling Charm", "incantation": "Rictusempra", "category": "CHARM", "difficulty": 2 }

### 9. A new professor (Wizard subtype: needs a subject), with a wand in the JSON attribute
# @name lockhart
POST {{api}}/professors
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Gilderoy Lockhart", "yearOfBirth": 1964, "subject": "Defence Against the Dark Arts",
  "wand": { "wood": "Cherry", "core": "Dragon heartstring", "lengthInches": 9 } }

### 10. Lockhart learns the Tickling Charm, badly
POST {{api}}/wizards/{{lockhart.response.body.$.id}}/spells
Content-Type: application/json

{ "spellId": "{{tickling.response.body.$.id}}", "level": 1, "favourite": true }

### 11. Level up (partial update of the link attributes)
PATCH {{api}}/wizards/{{lockhart.response.body.$.id}}/spells/{{tickling.response.body.$.id}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "level": 2 }

### ---- Errors ----

### 12. Unforgivable Curse below level 7 -> 422 hogwarts.unforgivableTooWeak (custom rule)
# @name crucio
GET {{api}}/views/spell-book?name=Crucio

###
POST {{api}}/wizards/{{lockhart.response.body.$.id}}/spells
Content-Type: application/json

{ "spellId": "{{crucio.response.body.$.items[0].id}}", "level": 3 }

### 13. Level outside 1-9 -> 400 validation (from the model's min/max)
POST {{api}}/wizards/{{lockhart.response.body.$.id}}/spells
Content-Type: application/json

{ "spellId": "{{crucio.response.body.$.items[0].id}}", "level": 10 }

### 14. Same spell twice -> 409 hogwarts.duplicateSpell
POST {{api}}/wizards/{{lockhart.response.body.$.id}}/spells
Content-Type: application/json

{ "spellId": "{{tickling.response.body.$.id}}", "level": 5 }

### 15. Unknown enum value -> 400 unreadable, lists the accepted categories
POST {{api}}/spells
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Prank Spell", "category": "PRANK" }

### 16. Professor without a subject -> 400 validation
POST {{api}}/professors
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Quirinus Quirrell" }

### 17. Duplicate name -> 409 duplicateName (unique constraint)
POST {{api}}/wizards
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Harry Potter" }

### 18. Delete a house that has members -> 409 hogwarts.houseNotEmpty (onDelete: restrict)
# @name houses
GET {{api}}/houses

###
DELETE {{api}}/houses/{{houses.response.body.$.items[0].id}}

### 19. Clean up: deleting Lockhart also deletes his spell links (cascade on the intersection)
DELETE {{api}}/wizards/{{lockhart.response.body.$.id}}
